186476864 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186476878 #edb/ref 1069 "q-68572" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186476878 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186476878 #edb/ref 1071 "$\\frac{\\sqrt[3]{16}}{\\sqrt[3]{2}}=$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186476878 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "0f503669-6b5c-5af4-8588-d775bd870f3b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186476878 #edb/ref 1074 "The quotient of cube roots of two numbers is equal to a cube root of the quotient of the numbers. Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\sqrt[3]{16}}{\\sqrt[3]{2}}=\\sqrt[3]{\\frac{16}{2}}=\\sqrt[3]{8}=2.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186476901 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186476786 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186476901 #edb/ref 1069 "q-152339" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186476901 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186476901 #edb/ref 1071 "Evaluate $\\frac{\\sqrt{32}}{\\sqrt{18}}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186476901 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "5b84391f-7419-5190-b6eb-dc760be50c2d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186476901 #edb/ref 1074 "A quotient of square roots of two positive numbers is equal to the square root of the quotient of the numbers. Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\sqrt{32}}{\\sqrt{18}}=\\sqrt{\\frac{32}{18}}=\\sqrt{\\frac{16}{9}}=\\sqrt{{(\\frac{4}{3})}^{2}}=\\frac{4}{3}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186476917 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186476822 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186476917 #edb/ref 1069 "q-99612" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186476917 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186476917 #edb/ref 1071 "$\\sqrt[3]{-\\frac{216}{343}}=$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186476917 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "7e8f9822-aefa-57f0-9acd-f132c358e3dc" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186476917 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we rewrite the fraction under the radical as follows:\n\n$$\n\\sqrt[3]{-\\frac{216}{343}}=\\sqrt[3]{\\frac{(-216)}{343}}\n$$\n\nThe cube root of a quotient of two numbers is equal to the quotient of the cube roots of the numbers. Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt[3]{\\frac{(-216)}{343}} & =\\frac{\\sqrt[3]{-216}}{\\sqrt[3]{343}} \\\\  & =\\frac{-6}{7} \\\\  & =-\\frac{6}{7}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186476934 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186476788 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186476934 #edb/ref 1069 "q-68560" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186476934 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186476934 #edb/ref 1071 "$\\frac{\\sqrt{8}}{\\sqrt{2}}=$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186476934 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "a94ec7d1-f4e5-51dc-8829-656b58e5dfc2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186476934 #edb/ref 1074 "A quotient of square roots of two positive numbers is equal to the square root of the quotient of the numbers. Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\sqrt{8}}{\\sqrt{2}}=\\sqrt{\\frac{8}{2}}=\\sqrt{4}=2.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186476939 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186476836 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186476939 #edb/ref 1069 "q-68994" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186476939 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186476939 #edb/ref 1071 "$\\sqrt{\\frac{7}{6}}=$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186476939 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "ac60cf99-8842-5103-9d62-b68e3fcaefa3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186476939 #edb/ref 1074 "The square root of a quotient of two positive numbers is equal to the quotient of the square roots of the numbers. Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\sqrt{\\frac{7}{6}}=\\frac{\\sqrt{7}}{\\sqrt{6}}.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186476952 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186476834 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186476952 #edb/ref 1069 "q-99595" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186476952 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186476952 #edb/ref 1071 "$\\frac{\\sqrt{28}}{\\sqrt{4}}=$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186476952 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "bb73c5d8-aabf-59ed-92d9-19dfc13a7e93" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186476952 #edb/ref 1074 "A quotient of square roots of two positive numbers is equal to the square root of the quotient of the numbers. Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\sqrt{28}}{\\sqrt{4}}=\\sqrt{\\frac{28}{4}}=\\sqrt{7}.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186476956 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186476804 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186476956 #edb/ref 1069 "q-152363" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186476956 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186476956 #edb/ref 1071 "$\\sqrt{\\frac{49}{3}}=$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186476956 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "be7dff0f-d441-5084-9288-7e04f3afc92e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186476956 #edb/ref 1074 "The square root of a quotient of two positive numbers is equal to the quotient of the square roots of the numbers. Therefore, \n\n$$\n\\sqrt{\\frac{49}{3}}=\\frac{\\sqrt{49}}{\\sqrt{3}}=\\frac{7}{\\sqrt{3}}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186476965 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186476798 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186476965 #edb/ref 1069 "q-152353" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186476965 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186476965 #edb/ref 1071 "Evaluate $\\frac{\\sqrt{48}}{\\sqrt{27}}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186476965 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "d878de54-991d-55eb-91a7-fd39612908df" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186476965 #edb/ref 1074 "A quotient of square roots of two positive numbers is equal to the square root of the quotient of the numbers. Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\sqrt{48}}{\\sqrt{27}}=\\sqrt{\\frac{48}{27}}=\\sqrt{\\frac{16}{9}}=\\sqrt{{(\\frac{4}{3})}^{2}}=\\frac{4}{3}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
